# Blank disk images: 288 MB of zeros across three files, recreated in one
# command each (see README). The v86 kernel and ISO beside them are NOT ignored,
# because they are only 25 MB and reproducing the exact build a measurement ran
# against is harder than storing it.
# A pattern containing a slash is anchored to this file's directory, so
# "images/blank-*.img" matched nothing under spike-b/ or spike-c/ and a 256 MB
# file sailed into the first commit. The leading ** is what makes it match at
# any depth.
**/images/blank-*.img

# Installed dependencies. v86 comes from npm; it is a dependency here, not
# something this repository redistributes.
node_modules/

# The manuscript is under review and is not published here. Nothing under
# paper/ is tracked: not the PDF, not the LaTeX source, not the bibliography,
# not the build scripts. They all stay local.
paper/

# Hand-made snapshots taken while editing. The *.bak rule below misses these
# because they end in .tex.
.bak*.tex

# Traces captured during a run, before they are curated into traces/.
trace.partial
*.partial.json

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor and script backups. One of these was committed before this rule existed.
*.bak
*.orig
*~
